{{also|blech}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|blëch}}, from {{inh|de|goh|bleh}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*blik}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*bliką}}. Compare {{cog|osx|blek}}, {{cog|nl|blik}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/blɛç/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Blech.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɛç|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n,s:es}}

# [[sheet]] (of metal)
# {{lb|de|informal}} any cheap, lightweight metal or metal object
# {{lb|de|informal|music|collective}} [[brass]] {{gloss|all brass instruments, or all brass players, etc.}}
#: {{ux|de|„Das '''Blech''' spielt bitte mal allein!“ rief der Dirigent.|The conductor demanded loudly: “'''Brass''' play on their own now, please!”}}

